        ":question/id": "681375a5-0c42-5d37-8f3f-a0f73ddc205e",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-101604",
        ":question/problem": "Given that $y=-9ln\u2061x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln\u2061x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-9ln\u2061x) \\\\  & =-9\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln\u2061x) \\\\  & =-9\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
