        ":question/problem": "Given that $y=2eln\u2061x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln\u2061x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2eln\u2061x) \\\\  & =2e\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln\u2061x) \\\\  & =2e\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2e}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
